---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import {defaults,limits} from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-06/solver.mjs';
const base='/equipment/03-06/', brochure='https://gammadata.se/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Fiji-G2-product-sheet-2018.pdf', uf='https://nrf.aux.eng.ufl.edu/_files/documents/19305.pdf#page=2';
const labels={diameterMm:'Disk diameter (mm)',heightMm:'Disk height (mm)',xMm:'Center offset X (mm)',yMm:'Center offset Y (mm)'};
---
<Layout pageTitle="Veeco Fiji G2 · static cabinet and teaching gauge" description="Inspect the exterior of a Fiji G2 model and validate clearance in an invented inert carrier gauge. This is not a deposition simulator." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment fj"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-06/">← Equipment 03-06</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#fj-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">03-06 · STATIC CABINET AND CARRIER FIT / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Veeco Fiji G2</h2><p>Inspect the cabinet and compare an inert teaching disk with an invented gauge. Nothing in this simulator operates the tool or processes material.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Load-lock configuration</h3><div id="fj-view" aria-label="Orbitable static Fiji G2 enclosure, tall tower, opaque reactor shell and top load-lock assembly"></div><div class="bar"><button data-fj-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-fj-view="gauge">Teaching-gauge close-up</button><button data-fj-view="rear">Cabinet rear</button><button id="fj-cutaway">Show teaching cutaway</button></div><p id="fj-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal marker shows an illustrative cutaway, not a real control or door.</p></section>
<section><h3>Independent static fit exercise</h3><canvas id="fj-diagram" width="700" height="330" aria-label="Inert disk and invented circular clearance gauge, independent of actual hardware tolerance"></canvas>
<div class="fields">{Object.entries(labels).map(([k,label])=><label>{label}<input id={'fj-'+k} type="number" min={limits[k][0]} max={limits[k][1]} step="any" value={defaults[k]}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="bar"><button id="fj-inspect" class="primary">Check static fit</button><button id="fj-carrier">Hide teaching disk</button><button id="fj-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="fj-status" aria-live="polite">Try the centered 200 mm disk, then an offset X = 3 mm, Y = 4 mm to see interference in this gauge.</p><output id="fj-result">No static fit report yet.</output><button id="fj-export" disabled>Export static-fit JSON</button></section></div>
<section id="fj-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3>
<p>Selected model: Veeco CNT Fiji G2 (not F200 or G2.2), nominal standard enclosed cabinet and Hine load-lock exterior from <a href={brochure+'#page=2'}>Veeco product sheet Rev. 7/18 p. 2</a>. The <a href={brochure+'#page=1'}>manufacturer front photograph, p. 1</a> and <a href={uf}>University of Florida NRF hardware photograph, p. 2</a> establish the cabinet, opaque upper assembly, and offset loading-area silhouette. No utilities, connections, internal process geometry or OEM access mechanism are modeled; rear detailing is inferred.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="650" height="450" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original front rendering of the closed non-operational white Fiji G2 cabinet"/><figcaption>Original rendering, not a photograph. Compared with manufacturer and university front views for overall assembly placement.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="650" height="450" src={base+'fit.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original teaching-only cutaway with an inert disk in an invented gauge"/><figcaption>Original synthetic teaching cutaway. The round seat is not a representation of real chamber interior, clearance, or loading operation.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Documented / reference</th><th>What the build uses</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Cabinet/assembly envelope</td><td>1845 × 715 × 1920 mm (length × depth × height), Rev. 7/18 p. 2</td><td>Nominal 1.845 × 0.715 × 1.920 m outer scale. Exterior parts not individually dimensioned are inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Invented clearance gauge</td><td>Radius 103 mm, height 10 mm</td><td>Simulation-only mathematical inputs, not manufactured specifications. Disk is a synthetic rigid cylinder.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Centered 200 × 4 mm disk</td><td>+3 mm radial, +6 mm vertical</td><td>Exact analytical fit in the invented gauge; tolerance 10⁻¹⁰ mm.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3,4 mm plane offset</td><td>5 mm center displacement; −2 mm radial margin</td><td>Interference in synthetic geometry, as expected.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register film/cycle acceptance</td><td>Complete and interrupted film cycle reference</td><td>Not applicable or run. No deposition, materials, chemistry, cycle controls, or witness-film claims.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Positive reserve means fit under the model, zero is contact, and negative denotes overlap. The math uses <code>lateral margin = Rgauge − Rdisk − hypot(x,y)</code> and <code>vertical margin = Hgauge − Hdisk</code>. Offsets are in the invented horizontal plane, in millimeters; no trajectory or physical loadability is evaluated. JSON preserves the input dimensions, proxy ID, revision, gauge provenance, margins, and model scope.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'fiji-g2-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-report.json'}>Output format example</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No physical instrument or immersive browser testing claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-06/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.fj{max-width:76rem}.fj .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.fj section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.fj .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.fj .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.fj label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.fj input,.fj button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.fj button{cursor:pointer}.fj button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.fj .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.fj #fj-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.fj #fj-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.fj #fj-diagram,.fj img{width:100%;height:auto}.fj #fj-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.fj #fj-status.error{color:#a54a34}.fj .scroll{overflow:auto}.fj table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.fj td,.fj th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.fj figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.fj .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
